the target language is: lps.

% A simplified loan agreement: real time, calendar dates, and a legal text
% behind every rule.
% Source: legacy_lps1/examples/CLOUT_workshop/loanAgreementPostConditionsRT*.pl,
% after Flood and Goodenough, "Contract as automaton".
%
% This is the first third of that contract -- request, advance, the annual
% payments and the potential default -- which is what exercises the constructs
% this program is here for. The real-time settings and the end_of_day poll live
% in the companion file loan_agreement.lps (docs/le_lps_surface.md §7).

the maximum time is 3200.

the events are:
    the day ends on *a date*; known as end_of_day.
    *a person* requests *an amount*; known as request.
    *a person* advances *an amount*; known as advance.
    *a payer* pays *an amount* to *a payee*; known as pay.
    *a person* notifies *a requirement*; known as notify.

the actions are:
    legal action is taken against *a person*; known as legal_action_against.
    the lender calls off the loan; known as cancel.
    *a person* falls into default; known as potential_default.

the fluents are:
    *a person* requested *an amount* on *a date*; known as requested.
    *a person* advanced *an amount* on *a date*; known as advanced.
    *a payer* paid *an amount* to *a payee* on *a date*; known as paid.
    *a person* was notified of *a requirement* on *a date*; known as notified.
    the assets exceed the liabilities; known as exceed_assets_liabilities.
    *a requirement* stands in default; known as potential_defaulted.
    *a requirement* has been cured; known as cured.
    the current date is *a date*; known as real_date.

the knowledge base loan agreement includes:

initially the assets exceed the liabilities.

% Clause 1. The borrower requests the advance, and the lender makes it.

when a person requests an amount
    and the current date is a date
then the person requested the amount on the date.

when a person advances an amount
    and the current date is a date
then the person advanced the amount on the date.

when a payer pays an amount to a payee
    and the current date is a date
then the payer paid the amount to the payee on the date.

when a person notifies a requirement
    and the current date is a date
then the person was notified of the requirement on the date.

% Clause 2. If the borrower has not requested by the agreed date, the loan is
% called off.

if the day ends on 2014-06-01 to a first time
    and it is not the case that borrower requested 1000 on 2014-06-01 at the first time
then the lender calls off the loan from the first time to a second time.

% Clause 3. If the lender has not advanced by the agreed date, the borrower may
% take legal action.

if the day ends on 2014-06-01 to a first time
    and borrower requested 1000 on 2014-06-01 at the first time
    and it is not the case that lender advanced 1000 on 2014-06-01 at the first time
then legal action is taken against lender from the first time to a second time.

% Clause 4. A missed annual payment is a potential default.

if the day ends on 2015-06-01 to a first time
    and it is not the case that borrower paid 550 to lender on 2015-06-01 at the first time
then borrower falls into default from the first time to a second time.

if the day ends on 2016-06-01 to a first time
    and it is not the case that borrower paid 525 to lender on 2016-06-01 at the first time
then borrower falls into default from the first time to a second time.

when a person falls into default
then the person stands in default.

% Clause 5. A representation that ceases to hold, and is not cured, is a
% default in its own right.

it must not be true that
    a payer pays an amount to a payee from a first time to a second time
    and the amount < 0.

scenario one is:
    borrower requests 1000 from 3 to 4.
    lender advances 1000 from 6 to 7.
    borrower pays 550 to lender from 1460 to 1461.
